  "id": "1c134157-7805-58b1-9a95-8e5ced668e7c",
  "slug": "sheet-pan-lasagna-recipe-11834200",
  "name": "Sheet Pan Lasagna",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This sheet pan lasagna saves the effort of layering and offers up more crispy edges, which we all know is the best part of lasagna. With sausage and a spinach-ricotta mixture, and cheese atop all, it's a fun way to make an old favorite.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Grease a 12x17-inch baking sheet with 1 to 2 tablespoons olive oil for a thin, crisp sheet-pan version, or use a 9x13-inch baking dish for a cozier, \u201cpasta bake\u201d feel."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Heat 1 tablespoon olive oil in a frying pan over medium heat. Add garlic and saut\u00e9 until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Add spinach and salt; cook, stirring, until wilted, about 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Transfer spinach to a bowl. Use kitchen shears to roughly chop, then stir in ricotta cheese. Set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Wipe out the frying pan with a paper towel. Add remaining 2 tablespoons olive oil and sausage. Cook undisturbed for 1 to 2 minutes to get some browning, then break sausage apart with a spatula. Continue cooking until browned throughout, about 5 minutes. Add red onion and saut\u00e9 until softened, about 3 minutes. Remove from heat."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, bring a large pot of salted water to a boil. Add lasagna sheets and cook for 4 minutes, stirring occasionally to prevent sticking. Drain and return to the pot. If you aren\u2019t immediately mixing with the sauce mixture (next step), toss pasta in a drizzle of olive oil to prevent sticking."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Stir marinara sauce into sausage mixture. Pour sausage and sauce into the pot with pasta. Add 1 1/2 cups mozzarella and 1 cup Parmesan, stirring until evenly coated."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Spread pasta mixture evenly on the prepared baking sheet or in the baking dish. Sprinkle remaining cheese on top. Spoon or dollop the spinach-ricotta mixture across the surface."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven, uncovered, until cheese is golden, sauce is bubbling, and edges are lightly crisped, about 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Serve warm with extra marinara sauce and a sprinkle of cheese, if desired. Enjoy!"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
